---

<Layout
  title="Twenty CRM Docker Deployment: Production Guide 2026"
  description="Step-by-step production deployment guide for self-hosting Twenty CRM on Linux using Docker Compose, PostgreSQL 16, Redis, and Caddy reverse proxy."
  canonical="https://opencrmstack.pages.dev/twenty-crm-self-hosted-docker-deployment-guide/"
  schemaJson={JSON.stringify(schema)}
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="text-xs text-slate-500 font-mono mb-6">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-emerald-400">OpenCRMStack</a> / <span>Self-Hosting</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-black text-white tracking-tight mb-6">
      Twenty CRM Self-Hosted Docker Compose Production Deployment Guide
    </h1>

    <div class="bg-emerald-950/20 border-l-4 border-l-emerald-500 border-y border-r border-emerald-500/30 rounded-xl p-6 shadow-xl mb-10">
      <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 font-mono mb-2">
        ⚡ Quick Answer: Deploying Twenty CRM Locally
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-200 leading-relaxed">
        <strong>Twenty CRM</strong> is the leading open-source modern alternative to HubSpot and Salesforce, built on TypeScript, NestJS, and PostgreSQL. Self-hosting requires deploying three containers via Docker Compose: the Twenty server image (<code>twentycrm/twenty:latest</code>), PostgreSQL 16 with UUID extensions, and Redis for background job queues. A single $10-$20/month VPS comfortably supports up to 25 sales representatives.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 1: Architecture Overview -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Architecture Overview &amp; Hardware Sizing</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-300 text-base leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Unlike legacy PHP CRMs (SuiteCRM, SugarCRM), Twenty is engineered with a modern multi-tier microservices architecture consisting of a GraphQL/REST API backend, BullMQ distributed task workers, and a React-based single-page application (SPA).
      </p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/60 mb-6">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300">
          <thead class="bg-slate-900 border-b border-slate-800 text-[11px] uppercase font-mono text-slate-400">
            <tr>
              <th class="p-3.5">Deployment Tier</th>
              <th class="p-3.5">Active Sales Seats</th>
              <th class="p-3.5">Recommended Hardware</th>
              <th class="p-3.5">Estimated Cloud Cost</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800/60 font-mono">
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-white font-sans">Starter Team</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 text-emerald-400">1 – 10 Seats</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 text-cyan-300">2 vCPU, 4GB RAM, 40GB NVMe</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 text-emerald-400">€7.50 / mo (Hetzner CPX21)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-white font-sans">Growth Organization</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 text-emerald-400">10 – 50 Seats</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 text-cyan-300">4 vCPU, 8GB RAM, 80GB NVMe</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 text-emerald-400">€14.90 / mo (Hetzner CPX31)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-white font-sans">Enterprise Fleet</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 text-emerald-400">50 – 250 Seats</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 text-cyan-300">8 vCPU, 16GB RAM, Dedicated DB</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 text-amber-300">€45.00 / mo (Managed Postgres)</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 2: Production Docker Compose Blueprint -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Production Docker Compose Specification</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Save the following configuration as <code>docker-compose.yml</code>. It includes database health checks, persistent volumes, and memory limits:
      </p>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/90 p-4 font-mono text-xs text-cyan-300 overflow-x-auto mb-6">
        <pre is:raw>
version: '3.8'

services:
  twenty-server:
    image: twentycrm/twenty:latest
    container_name: twenty-server
    restart: unless-stopped
    ports:
      - "127.0.0.1:3000:3000"
    environment:
      - PORT=3000
      - NODE_ENV=production
      - PG_DATABASE_URL=postgres://twenty:SuperSecretDBPass2026@twenty-db:5432/twenty
      - REDIS_URL=redis://twenty-redis:6379
      - SIGNING_KEY=a7f4e8b1c9d2358e601249abcdf0382910485762019384756102938475610293
      - SERVER_URL=https://crm.yourdomain.com
      - STORAGE_TYPE=local
      - STORAGE_LOCAL_PATH=/app/packages/twenty-server/.local-storage
    volumes:
      - twenty_server_data:/app/packages/twenty-server/.local-storage
    depends_on:
      twenty-db:
        condition: service_healthy
      twenty-redis:
        condition: service_started
    healthcheck:
      test: ["CMD", "curl", "-f", "http://localhost:3000/healthz"]
      interval: 10s
      timeout: 5s
      retries: 5

  twenty-db:
    image: postgres:16-alpine
    container_name: twenty-db
    restart: unless-stopped
    environment:
      - POSTGRES_USER=twenty
      - POSTGRES_PASSWORD=SuperSecretDBPass2026
      - POSTGRES_DB=twenty
      - PGDATA=/var/lib/postgresql/data/pgdata
    volumes:
      - twenty_db_data:/var/lib/postgresql/data
    healthcheck:
      test: ["CMD-SHELL", "pg_isready -U twenty -d twenty"]
      interval: 5s
      timeout: 5s
      retries: 5

  twenty-redis:
    image: redis:7-alpine
    container_name: twenty-redis
    restart: unless-stopped
    command: redis-server --appendonly yes
    volumes:
      - twenty_redis_data:/data

volumes:
  twenty_server_data:
  twenty_db_data:
  twenty_redis_data:
        </pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 3: SSL Reverse Proxy with Caddy -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">SSL &amp; Domain Reverse Proxy Configuration</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
        To terminate SSL and enable HTTP/3 acceleration, expose Twenty via Caddy. Create <code>/etc/caddy/Caddyfile</code>:
      </p>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/90 p-4 font-mono text-xs text-emerald-400 overflow-x-auto mb-6">
        <pre is:raw>
crm.yourdomain.com {
    encode gzip zstd

    # Forward traffic to Twenty container
    reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3000 {
        header_up Host {host}
        header_up X-Real-IP {remote_host}
        header_up X-Forwarded-Proto {scheme}
    }

    # Security Headers
    header {
        Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload"
        X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
        X-Frame-Options "SAMEORIGIN"
    }
}
        </pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 4: Automated S3 Backups & Disaster Recovery -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Automated Database Backups &amp; Disaster Recovery</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-300 text-base leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Never operate production CRM data without automated off-site backups. Set up a daily cron job that dumps the PostgreSQL database, compresses it with zstd, and uploads to Cloudflare R2 (zero egress fees):
      </p>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/90 p-4 font-mono text-xs text-slate-200 overflow-x-auto mb-6">
        <pre is:raw>
#!/bin/bash
# /opt/scripts/backup_twenty.sh
BACKUP_DIR="/var/backups/twenty"
TIMESTAMP=$(date +%Y%m%d_%H%M%S)
FILENAME="twenty_db_${TIMESTAMP}.sql.zst"

mkdir -p ${BACKUP_DIR}

# Dump and compress
docker exec twenty-db pg_dump -U twenty twenty | zstd -3 > "${BACKUP_DIR}/${FILENAME}"

# Sync to S3-compatible storage (Cloudflare R2)
rclone copy "${BACKUP_DIR}/${FILENAME}" "r2:crm-backups/daily/"

# Prune local backups older than 7 days
find ${BACKUP_DIR} -type f -name "*.sql.zst" -mtime +7 -delete
        </pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 5: Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) vs HubSpot -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Total Cost of Ownership (TCO): Twenty vs HubSpot Sales Hub</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/60 mb-6">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300">
          <thead class="bg-slate-900 border-b border-slate-800 text-[11px] uppercase font-mono text-slate-400">
            <tr>
              <th class="p-3.5">Expense Item</th>
              <th class="p-3.5">Self-Hosted Twenty CRM (15 Users)</th>
              <th class="p-3.5">HubSpot Sales Hub Professional (15 Users)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800/60 font-mono">
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-white font-sans">Monthly Software License</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 text-emerald-400 font-bold">$0.00 (AGPLv3)</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 text-rose-400 font-bold">$1,500.00 / month ($100/seat)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-white font-sans">Cloud Infrastructure (VPS + S3)</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 text-cyan-300">$12.50 / month</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 text-slate-400">Included in subscription</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-white font-sans">Mandatory Onboarding Fee</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 text-emerald-400">$0.00</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 text-rose-400">$1,500.00 one-time fee</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-white font-sans">Annual Total Cost</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 text-emerald-400 font-bold">$150.00 / year</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 text-rose-400 font-bold">$19,500.00 / year</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 font-mono">
        *Self-hosting Twenty CRM delivers a <strong>99.2% annual cost reduction</strong> while keeping 100% of sensitive customer contact data and deal values on self-controlled sovereign hardware.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 6: Frequently Asked Questions -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800">
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white mb-2">What hardware specifications are required to self-host Twenty CRM?</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            For teams up to 25 active sales representatives, a standard Linux VPS with 2 vCPUs, 4GB RAM, and 50GB NVMe storage (e.g. Hetzner CPX21 for ~€8/month) is optimal. Twenty server requires ~1.2GB RAM, PostgreSQL takes ~800MB, and Redis takes ~150MB.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800">
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white mb-2">How does Twenty CRM handle email synchronization and calendar integrations?</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Twenty CRM provides native Google Workspace and Microsoft 365 OAuth integrations using background worker queues managed via Redis and BullMQ, supporting two-way calendar and email thread sync.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800">
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white mb-2">Can Twenty CRM be deployed with automated daily database backups?</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Yes. A secondary backup container using pg_dump running a daily cron exports encrypted SQL dumps to an S3-compatible bucket (Cloudflare R2 or AWS S3) with automated 30-day retention policies.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="p-6 rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/40 mt-10">
      <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Explore related open-source CRM blueprints: <a href="/twenty-crm-vs-hubspot-open-source-sales-pipeline-audit/" class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline">Twenty CRM vs HubSpot Audit</a>, <a href="/espocrm-vs-suitecrm-lightweight-php-open-source/" class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline">EspoCRM vs SuiteCRM Shootout</a>, and <a href="/self-hosted-erpnext-vs-salesforce-cost-migration-breakdown/" class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline">ERPNext vs Salesforce Migration</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>\n